  "name": "Graveyard field tiles",
  "notes": "8x8 tiles of the night meadow. Solid: the forest canopy. 'W'/'w' are deep forest; 'A'-'O' are canopy edges with a round leafy rim on every side that faces open ground (moonlit top-left, shaded bottom-right), so tree clumps read as round crowns. Scenery (walk over it): '_' canopy shadow on the grass, '|' '(' ')' tree trunks under the crowns, '1'-'8' grass blades (denser = darker patches), 'q'-'v' lighter moonlit grass, ',' ';' tufts, '*' '%' flowers, 'o' pebbles, '+' 't' 'n' headstones (round, cross, small), 'm' grave plot, 'b' bone, 'k' skull. Ground texture stays low-contrast so monsters and gems stay easy to see.",
